Replace with overlay styles. Also ensure `.battle-unit` has gap 2px but only figure now; no issue.

Let's craft:

```css
.unit-labels {
  position: absolute;
  z-index: 12;
  inset: 0;
  overflow: hidden;
  pointer-events: none;
}

.unit-label {
  position: absolute;
  left: calc(var(--x) * 1%);
  top: calc(var(--y) * 1%);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 2px;
  transform: translate(-50%, -100%);
  transition: opacity 0.3s ease;
}

.unit-label.hero {
  --lift: clamp(57.5px, 17.5vw, 77.5px);
  transform: translate(calc(-50% - 7px), calc(-100% - var(--lift) - 3px));
}

.unit-label.enemy {
  --lift: clamp(42px, 12.5vw, 56px);
  transform: translate(calc(-50% + 7px), calc(-100% - var(--lift) - 3px));
}

.unit-label.enemy.boss {
  --lift: clamp(64px, 19vw, 88px);
}

.unit-label .label-name {
  max-width: 78px;
  overflow: hidden;
  padding: 0 3px;
  color: #dbcdb9;
  font-size: 6.5px;
  font-weight: 900;
  letter-spacing: .03em;
  line-height: 1;
  text-align: center;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  text-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.95), 0 0 6px rgba(0,0,0,.75);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.unit-label.dead,
.unit-label.dying {
  opacity: 0;
}
```

Note `.unit-label` display flex column with align-items center; names above bar. For enemy, no name, just bar.

